      "execution": {
        "startingPosition": "Lie with your upper back firmly on the floor, a padded barbell across your hips, your feet shoulder-width apart, and your knees bent near 115 degrees. Steady the bar with your palms facing up.",
        "movement": "Raise your pelvis.",
        "endpoint": "End the lift when your body forms a straight line from shoulders to knees with your knees bent near 115 degrees.",
        "returnPhase": "Lower until the plates return to the floor without shifting your upper torso, arching your back, or letting your knees drift outward.",
        "controlledJoints": "Keep your upper back firmly on the floor and both feet planted.",
        "supportAndPosture": "Support your upper back on the floor and brace your trunk.",
        "disqualifyingCompensations": [
          "Setting the feet so the knees finish near 90 degrees turns the glute bridge into a hip thrust.",
          "Letting the knees drift outward turns the glute bridge into a frog pump.",
          "Arching the back to push past a straight line turns the glute bridge into a back hyperextension."
